      "id": "sol.hmmt-nov-general-1-2009-p3.hmmt",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "\\(\\pi\\) Since \\(f(x)\\) never equals \\(\\cos (1)\\) for \\(x \\in(0, \\pi)\\) but \\(f(0)=\\cos (1)\\), the period is at least \\(\\pi\\). However, \\(\\cos (x+\\pi)=-\\cos (x)\\), so \\(\\cos (\\cos (x+\\pi))=\\cos (\\cos (x))\\).",
